      <p class="mgc-result">
        <span class="mgc-result-highlight">Plan G annual cost: $1,440 premiums + $257 Part B deductible = $1,697 total</span>
        <span class="mgc-result-highlight">Plan N annual cost: $1,104 premiums + $257 deductible + $40 copays = $1,401 total</span>
      </p>
      <p class="mgc-action">Dorothy chose Plan N, saving about $296 per year in her low-use situation. She understood she could switch to Plan G later only if she remains healthy enough to pass medical underwriting.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Scenario 2 -->
