      <table class="mgc-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Input</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Age at enrollment</td><td>68</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Expected specialist visits per year</td><td>4–6 cardiologist visits + 1 procedure</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Plan G monthly premium (estimate)</td><td>$155/month</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Plan N copay exposure per year</td><td>$120+ (6 visits × $20)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="mgc-result">
        <span class="mgc-result-highlight">Plan G annual cost: $1,860 premiums + $257 deductible = $2,117 total, zero unpredictable bills</span>
        <span class="mgc-result-highlight">Plan N annual cost: $1,428 premiums + $257 deductible + $120+ copays = $1,805+ total</span>
      </p>
      <p class="mgc-action">Harold chose Plan G for the peace of mind of zero copays. The $312 annual premium savings from Plan N was not worth the constant copay tracking and the risk that his cardiologist charges Part B excess charges.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Scenario 3 -->
    <div class="mgc-scenario-card">
      <div class="mgc-scenario-header">
        <span class="mgc-scenario-tag">Example 3</span>
        <strong class="mgc-scenario-name">Ruth, 74 — Longtime Medicare Advantage Member Switching to Original Medicare</strong>
      </div>
      <p class="mgc-scenario-desc">Ruth left Medicare Advantage after 7 years due to constant prior authorization delays. She is switching to Original Medicare plus Medigap but needs to pass health underwriting since her Medigap Open Enrollment window closed years ago.</p>
      <table class="mgc-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Input</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
